# Closed complete role census checks

The fixed runner checks current source contracts and non-ignored component tests
on Windows and local Ubuntu Rust 1.94 / MSRV 1.88. It never dispatches a unit,
original attempt, measurement, or server operation. Synthetic kernel tests own
and reap their own children. Existing services and clocks are unchanged.

```powershell
python -B -m unittest discover -s tools/held-complete-census-074 -v
python -B tools/held-complete-census-074/check.py host
python -B tools/held-complete-census-074/check.py 194
python -B tools/held-complete-census-074/check.py 188
python -B tools/held-complete-census-074/check.py controls-v2
python -B tools/held-complete-census-074/check.py docs-v2
```

Receipts are exclusive under target/held-complete-census-20261022; an existing
lane refuses before execution. Do not rerun a failed lane to replace its outcome.
Each command retains argv, raw streams, exit status and source digests. Elapsed
compile/test time is operational metadata, not a performance measurement.

After independent documentation checks have been recorded in the docs subfolder,
retain.py requires all fixed lanes, exact commands and source/log hashes, the
red baseline, nine new component tests per compiler, 17 material and ten
projection regressions, and the unchanged qualification hash. It compares sources
with the supplied committed runtime, then creates a new packet and inventory
exclusively. The initial component failure is retained as a development summary,
not falsely presented as an original raw process receipt.

The result is a private 11-role value binding and 23-entry descriptor-number
census, not a universal all-writer census or permission to send or execute.
